# Ingestion Pipeline Conventions

## Prompt Strategy

Use **separate prompts per content type**:

| Type      | Purpose                                  |
|-----------|------------------------------------------|
| `NEWS`    | Articles, interviews, announcements      |
| `RELEASE` | Albums, singles, EPs, music videos       |
| `EVENT`   | Concerts, festivals, tour dates (fallback when structured provider has no data) |

## JSON Extraction Contract

Every prompt must return a **strict JSON array** matching the content-type schema. Validate the response with Zod before storing. Discard any item that fails validation rather than attempting to repair it.

## Time Windows

- **First run:** 30-day backfill per artist.
- **Subsequent runs:** Incremental, fetching only items since the last successful run.

## Confidence Threshold

A global `MIN_CONFIDENCE` setting controls the minimum confidence score. Items scoring below this threshold are discarded before insert.

## Dedupe

Before inserting, compute `hash(type + artistId + normalizedUrl)` and skip if the hash already exists. This prevents duplicate items across overlapping search results or re-runs.

## Testability

All OpenAI and event-provider calls go through injectable interfaces (see `development-standards.mdc`). Tests use stubs that return canned JSON — never call real APIs.
